# Vulnerabilities accepted, with the reason and the condition for revisiting.
#
# An entry here is a claim that the finding is not reachable in this codebase --
# not that it is inconvenient. Each one names what makes it unreachable, so the
# claim can be checked rather than trusted.

# CVE-2026-85061 -- maplibre-gl, CVSS 10 XSS in DOM.sanitize()
#
# The flaw: DOM.sanitize() iterates a live NamedNodeMap while removing
# attributes, so removing one shifts the rest and an adjacent `onload`/`ontoggle`
# can survive. It is reached through *attribution strings* -- either an untrusted
# third-party style's attribution, or a user-supplied custom one -- which the
# attribution control then writes with innerHTML. Fixed in 6.4.1.
#
# Why it is not reachable here:
#
#   1. This app renders exactly one attribution string, and it is a literal in
#      our own source (`buildStyle` in frontend/src/features/map/basemap.ts).
#      No user, style, or remote document can influence it.
#   2. The one path by which third-party content could have reached the control
#      -- the .pmtiles archive's own metadata attribution -- is now explicitly
#      disabled with `new Protocol({ metadata: false })`. It was already inert,
#      because pmtiles only reads that flag for TileJSON (`type === "json"`)
#      requests and the style uses the explicit `tiles: [...]` template form,
#      but it is now off by intent rather than by accident.
#   3. There is no custom attribution API exposed to users anywhere in the app.
#
# Why not simply upgrade, which is what you should normally do:
#
#   MapLibre is pinned to 5.x because pmtiles 4.5 -- still the latest release --
#   does not work against MapLibre 6. Re-tested on 2026-09-10 against both 6.4.1
#   (the minimum patched version) and 6.9.0: in each case zero tile range
#   requests are issued, the vector source stays pending forever, `load` never
#   fires, and so the pins query never enables either. The map does not degrade,
#   it dies -- basemap *and* markers. Upgrading to clear this CVE would trade a
#   non-reachable XSS for a wholly broken map.
#
# Revisit when: pmtiles ships MapLibre 6 support (watch its peerDependencies and
# release notes), or if this app ever renders an attribution string it does not
# author itself. Either change invalidates the reasoning above.
CVE-2026-85061
